#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "What the script does"
msgstr "Co skript provede"

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "If Oracle has no free capacity"
msgstr "Pokud Oracle nemá volnou kapacitu"

#~ msgid "Ampere A1 servers are popular and regions often run out. The installer tries every availability domain in your region and keeps retrying for 30 minutes. It already asks for the smallest size the installer offers, 1 core and 6 GB, so there is nothing smaller to fall back to. If it gives up, run the command again later: it remembers your domain, so the command no longer needs it, and everything already created is reused. Upgrading to Pay As You Go also tends to end these errors, since paying accounts are served first when servers are scarce."
#~ msgstr "Ampere A1 servers are popular and regions often run out. The installer tries every availability domain in your region and keeps retrying for 30 minutes. It already asks for the smallest size the installer offers, 1 core and 6 GB, so there is nothing smaller to fall back to. If it gives up, run the command again later: it remembers your domain, so the command no longer needs it, and everything already created is reused. Upgrading to Pay As You Go also tends to end these errors, since paying accounts are served first when servers are scarce."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "To have it keep trying for longer instead of re-running by hand:"
msgstr "Chcete-li prodloužit dobu opakování pokusů místo ručního opětovného spuštění:"

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "If anything goes wrong, run it again"
msgstr "Pokud se něco pokazí, spusťte jej znovu"

#~ msgid "Running the installer a second time is the fix for almost any failure. It looks every resource up before creating it, and checks the server itself on every run, so a run that was interrupted or stopped part-way carries on from where it got to rather than starting over. It remembers your domain, so the command on its own is enough."
#~ msgstr "Running the installer a second time is the fix for almost any failure. It looks every resource up before creating it, and checks the server itself on every run, so a run that was interrupted or stopped part-way carries on from where it got to rather than starting over. It remembers your domain, so the command on its own is enough."

#~ msgid "The script ends by printing your <0>instance key</0>. It is the master credential for this installation, used for administrative API access and account recovery. Save it in a password manager. Running the script again shows it again."
#~ msgstr "The script ends by printing your <0>instance key</0>. It is the master credential for this installation, used for administrative API access and account recovery. Save it in a password manager. Running the script again shows it again."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Download the SSH key the script created. It lives only in your Cloud Shell home, which Oracle deletes after six months without a Cloud Shell session. Use the Cloud Shell menu, <0>Download</0>, and enter <1/>. Nocturne keeps running without it, but it is your only way onto the server."
msgstr "Stáhněte klíč SSH vytvořený skriptem. Nachází se pouze ve vašem domovském adresáři Cloud Shell, který Oracle po šesti měsících bez relace Cloud Shell smaže. V nabídce Cloud Shell zvolte <0>Download</0> a zadejte <1/>. Nocturne poběží i bez něj, ale klíč je jediným způsobem, jak se dostat na server."

#~ msgid "Updates are automatic. Watchtower checks for new Nocturne images daily."
#~ msgstr "Updates are automatic. Watchtower checks for new Nocturne images daily."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Nocturne starts again by itself when the server reboots."
msgstr "Po restartu serveru se Nocturne automaticky znovu spustí."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "To get a shell on the server, run the SSH command the script printed. Everything lives in <0/>."
msgstr "Chcete-li otevřít shell na serveru, spusťte příkaz SSH vypsaný skriptem. Všechny soubory jsou v <0/>."

#~ msgid "Nothing backs up your data automatically. In the Oracle console, under Block Storage, you can take a backup of the server's boot volume at any time. The free tier includes five volume backups, so take them by hand and delete old ones rather than attaching a scheduled policy."
#~ msgstr "Nothing backs up your data automatically. In the Oracle console, under Block Storage, you can take a backup of the server's boot volume at any time. The free tier includes five volume backups, so take them by hand and delete old ones rather than attaching a scheduled policy."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "To remove everything, terminate the instance in the Oracle console, then delete the reserved public IP and the <0>nocturne</0> virtual cloud network."
msgstr "Chcete-li vše odstranit, ukončete instanci v konzoli Oracle a potom smažte rezervovanou veřejnou IP adresu a virtuální cloudovou síť <0>nocturne</0>."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Run Nocturne on Oracle Cloud's Always Free tier. One command in the browser sets up the server, the network, HTTPS and Nocturne itself. No SSH or Docker knowledge needed."
msgstr "Spusťte Nocturne v bezplatném tarifu Always Free služby Oracle Cloud. Jediný příkaz v prohlížeči nastaví server, síť, HTTPS i samotné Nocturne. Nepotřebujete znát SSH ani Docker."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "What you need"
msgstr "Co budete potřebovat"

#~ msgid "No domain yet? Get one from deSEC"
#~ msgstr "No domain yet? Get one from deSEC"

#~ msgid "<0>deSEC</0> is a non-profit DNS provider that gives out free names under <1>dedyn.io</1>. With one of those, the installer creates the DNS records for you and there is nothing to configure by hand."
#~ msgstr "<0>deSEC</0> is a non-profit DNS provider that gives out free names under <1>dedyn.io</1>. With one of those, the installer creates the DNS records for you and there is nothing to configure by hand."

#~ msgid "The same works for a domain you already own if its DNS is hosted at deSEC. If it is hosted elsewhere, you add two records by hand in Step 3."
#~ msgstr "The same works for a domain you already own if its DNS is hosted at deSEC. If it is hosted elsewhere, you add two records by hand in Step 3."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Before you start: keeping it free"
msgstr "Než začnete: jak zůstat v bezplatném tarifu"

#~ msgid "Oracle switches off Always Free servers on trial accounts that it judges idle for seven days in a row. Its measure is whether the processor, network and memory each stayed below 20 percent of capacity for nearly all of that week. A Nocturne server for one person does very little work by that yardstick, so left alone it is likely to be stopped after its first quiet week. There are two ways to prevent that, and one of them changes the command in Step 2, so pick now rather than later."
#~ msgstr "Oracle switches off Always Free servers on trial accounts that it judges idle for seven days in a row. Its measure is whether the processor, network and memory each stayed below 20 percent of capacity for nearly all of that week. A Nocturne server for one person does very little work by that yardstick, so left alone it is likely to be stopped after its first quiet week. There are two ways to prevent that, and one of them changes the command in Step 2, so pick now rather than later."

#~ msgid "Pay As You Go suits most people: it is a single change in the Oracle console, adds nothing to the server, and paying accounts are served first when Ampere capacity is scarce. The trade-off is that the card already on file <0>can</0> be charged if anything outside the free allowance is ever created. Choose Folding@home instead if you would rather the account stay a trial that cannot be billed at all, and you do not mind a second piece of software with network access on the server that holds your health data."
#~ msgstr "Pay As You Go suits most people: it is a single change in the Oracle console, adds nothing to the server, and paying accounts are served first when Ampere capacity is scarce. The trade-off is that the card already on file <0>can</0> be charged if anything outside the free allowance is ever created. Choose Folding@home instead if you would rather the account stay a trial that cannot be billed at all, and you do not mind a second piece of software with network access on the server that holds your health data."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Step 1: Open Cloud Shell"
msgstr "Krok 1: Otevřete Cloud Shell"

#~ msgid "Sign in to the <0>Oracle Cloud console</0> and click the terminal icon in the top-right toolbar, labelled <1>Developer tools</1>, then <2>Cloud Shell</2>. A terminal opens at the bottom of the page. It is already signed in as you, so there is nothing to install or configure."
#~ msgstr "Sign in to the <0>Oracle Cloud console</0> and click the terminal icon in the top-right toolbar, labelled <1>Developer tools</1>, then <2>Cloud Shell</2>. A terminal opens at the bottom of the page. It is already signed in as you, so there is nothing to install or configure."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Step 2: Run the installer"
msgstr "Krok 2: Spusťte instalátor"

#~ msgid "Paste this into Cloud Shell, replacing <0/> with your domain. Nocturne will answer on that name and every site you create gets a subdomain under it, so pick something you are happy to keep. If you chose Folding@home above, add <1/> in front."
#~ msgstr "Paste this into Cloud Shell, replacing <0/> with your domain. Nocturne will answer on that name and every site you create gets a subdomain under it, so pick something you are happy to keep. If you chose Folding@home above, add <1/> in front."

#~ msgid "Early on it asks for a deSEC token. <0>Nothing appears on screen as you paste it</0> — the token is hidden, and the installer tells you how many characters it read so you can see the paste landed. If deSEC does not accept it you can paste another. Press Enter with nothing pasted and it prints two records for you to create by hand instead. Either way it keeps working while the server boots, and waits for the records before it requests certificates."
#~ msgstr "Early on it asks for a deSEC token. <0>Nothing appears on screen as you paste it</0> — the token is hidden, and the installer tells you how many characters it read so you can see the paste landed. If deSEC does not accept it you can paste another. Press Enter with nothing pasted and it prints two records for you to create by hand instead. Either way it keeps working while the server boots, and waits for the records before it requests certificates."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Step 3: Add the DNS records"
msgstr "Krok 3: Přidejte záznamy DNS"

