#~ msgid "Watchtower checks for new Nocturne images daily. It does not update Caddy or Postgres; update them with <0/>."
#~ msgstr "Watchtower checks for new Nocturne images daily. It does not update Caddy or Postgres; update them with <0/>."

#~ msgid "An <0>Oracle Cloud account</0>. Sign-up asks for a payment card to verify your identity. The region you pick at sign-up becomes your home region. The free server can only be created there, and the choice cannot be changed later, so pick the region closest to you. Always Free gives you 2 Ampere cores, 12 GB of memory and 200 GB of storage. Oracle halved the cores and memory in June 2026, so older guides that quote 4 cores and 24 GB are out of date. This guide uses half the cores and memory and a quarter of the storage, which stays well inside the free allowance."
#~ msgstr "An <0>Oracle Cloud account</0>. Sign-up asks for a payment card to verify your identity. The region you pick at sign-up becomes your home region. The free server can only be created there, and the choice cannot be changed later, so pick the region closest to you. Always Free gives you 2 Ampere cores, 12 GB of memory and 200 GB of storage. Oracle halved the cores and memory in June 2026, so older guides that quote 4 cores and 24 GB are out of date. This guide uses half the cores and memory and a quarter of the storage, which stays well inside the free allowance."

#~ msgid "A domain name. Nocturne gives every site its own subdomain, so the DNS provider must support wildcard records. If you do not have a domain, a free one from DuckDNS works well; <0>see below</0>."
#~ msgstr "A domain name. Nocturne gives every site its own subdomain, so the DNS provider must support wildcard records. If you do not have a domain, a free one from DuckDNS works well; <0>see below</0>."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Sign in at duckdns.org with one of the accounts it offers, such as GitHub or Google."
msgstr "Přihlaste se na duckdns.org pomocí některého z nabízených účtů, například GitHubu nebo Google."

#~ msgid "Under <0>domains</0>, type a name and click <1>add domain</1>. Your domain is then <2/>."
#~ msgstr "Under <0>domains</0>, type a name and click <1>add domain</1>. Your domain is then <2/>."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Copy the <0>token</0> shown at the top of the page. It looks like <1/>. It controls every name on your account, so keep it to yourself."
msgstr "Zkopírujte <0>token</0> zobrazený v horní části stránky. Vypadá takto: <1/>. Umožňuje spravovat všechny názvy ve vašem účtu, proto ho nikomu nesdělujte."

#~ msgid "What changes is that the card can now be charged if something outside the free tier is ever created. The installer closes that off from both ends: it refuses a server size above the free allowance, and it writes an Oracle quota policy that stops the account creating anything outside the Always Free compute shapes at all, whether or not you have upgraded. That policy is a real limit rather than a warning: Oracle refuses the request instead of billing you for it. The installer also sets a spending alert that emails you the moment the account is billed one unit of your currency. Nothing needs adding to the command in <0>Step 2</0>."
#~ msgstr "What changes is that the card can now be charged if something outside the free tier is ever created. The installer closes that off from both ends: it refuses a server size above the free allowance, and it writes an Oracle quota policy that stops the account creating anything outside the Always Free compute shapes at all, whether or not you have upgraded. That policy is a real limit rather than a warning: Oracle refuses the request instead of billing you for it. The installer also sets a spending alert that emails you the moment the account is billed one unit of your currency. Nothing needs adding to the command in <0>Step 2</0>."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Option 2: stay on an Always Free account and donate spare time to Folding@home"
msgstr "Možnost 2: ponechat si účet Always Free a věnovat nevyužitý výpočetní výkon projektu Folding@home"

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "The client runs at the lowest priority the system has, so Nocturne and its alarms always come first. To choose this option, add <0/> to the command in <1>Step 2</1>:"
msgstr "Klient běží s nejnižší systémovou prioritou, takže Nocturne a jeho alarmy mají vždy přednost. Chcete-li zvolit tuto možnost, přidejte <0/> k příkazu v <1>kroku 2</1>:"

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "Work is contributed anonymously by default. To count it towards a team, add <0/> as well. Always Free accounts cannot be charged, but the installer still creates the spending alert in case the account is upgraded later."
msgstr "Výpočetní práce se standardně poskytuje anonymně. Chcete-li ji započítat týmu, přidejte také <0/>. Účtům Always Free nelze nic naúčtovat, instalátor však vytvoří upozornění na výdaje pro případ, že účet později převedete na vyšší tarif."

#~ msgid "Points your DuckDNS name at that address when you give it the token; for any other domain, it prints the two records to create by hand"
#~ msgstr "Points your DuckDNS name at that address when you give it the token; for any other domain, it prints the two records to create by hand"

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "The script ends by printing your <0>instance key</0>. It is the master credential for this installation, used for administrative API access and account recovery. Save it in a password manager. Running the script a second time prints it once more."
msgstr "Skript na konci vypíše <0>klíč instance</0>. Jde o hlavní přihlašovací údaj k této instalaci, který slouží ke správě přes API a obnově účtu. Uložte ho do správce hesel. Opětovné spuštění skriptu klíč vypíše ještě jednou."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "To update Caddy and Postgres, run <0/> on the server."
msgstr "Chcete-li aktualizovat Caddy a Postgres, spusťte na serveru <0/>."

#~ msgid "Nothing backs up your data automatically. In the Oracle console, under Block Storage, you can take a backup of the server's boot volume at any time. The free tier includes five volume backups, so take them by hand and delete old ones rather than attaching a scheduled policy, which would keep more than five and be charged."
#~ msgstr "Nothing backs up your data automatically. In the Oracle console, under Block Storage, you can take a backup of the server's boot volume at any time. The free tier includes five volume backups, so take them by hand and delete old ones rather than attaching a scheduled policy, which would keep more than five and be charged."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "No domain yet? Get one from DuckDNS"
msgstr "Ještě nemáte doménu? Získejte ji přes DuckDNS"

#~ msgid "<0>DuckDNS</0> is a free dynamic DNS service that gives out names under <1>duckdns.org</1>, each with a wildcard for the subdomains below it. The installer uses your DuckDNS token to point your name at your server, so there is nothing to set up by hand."
#~ msgstr "<0>DuckDNS</0> is a free dynamic DNS service that gives out names under <1>duckdns.org</1>, each with a wildcard for the subdomains below it. The installer uses your DuckDNS token to point your name at your server, so there is nothing to set up by hand."

#: ../portal/src/routes/docs/installation/oracle-cloud/+page.svelte
msgid "For a domain you already own, you add two records by hand at your DNS provider in <0>Step 3</0>."
msgstr "Pokud už vlastníte doménu, v <0>kroku 3</0> ručně přidejte dva záznamy u svého poskytovatele DNS."

#~ msgid "Oracle switches off servers on Always Free accounts that it judges idle for seven days in a row. Its measure is whether the processor, network and memory each stayed below 20 percent of capacity for nearly all of that week. A Nocturne server for one person does very little work by that yardstick, so left alone it is likely to be stopped after its first quiet week. There are two ways to prevent that, and one of them changes the command in <0>Step 2</0>, so pick now rather than later."
#~ msgstr "Oracle switches off servers on Always Free accounts that it judges idle for seven days in a row. Its measure is whether the processor, network and memory each stayed below 20 percent of capacity for nearly all of that week. A Nocturne server for one person does very little work by that yardstick, so left alone it is likely to be stopped after its first quiet week. There are two ways to prevent that, and one of them changes the command in <0>Step 2</0>, so pick now rather than later."

#~ msgid "Pay As You Go suits most people: it is a single change in the Oracle console, adds nothing to the server, and paying accounts are served first when Ampere capacity is scarce. The trade-off is that the card already on file <0>can</0> be charged if anything outside the free allowance is ever created. Choose Folding@home instead if you would rather keep an Always Free account that cannot be billed at all, and you do not mind a second piece of software with network access on the server that holds your health data."
#~ msgstr "Pay As You Go suits most people: it is a single change in the Oracle console, adds nothing to the server, and paying accounts are served first when Ampere capacity is scarce. The trade-off is that the card already on file <0>can</0> be charged if anything outside the free allowance is ever created. Choose Folding@home instead if you would rather keep an Always Free account that cannot be billed at all, and you do not mind a second piece of software with network access on the server that holds your health data."

#~ msgid "Paste this into Cloud Shell, replacing <0/> with your domain, such as <1/>. Nocturne will answer on that name and every site you create gets a subdomain under it, so pick something you are happy to keep. If you chose Folding@home above, add <2/> in front."
#~ msgstr "Paste this into Cloud Shell, replacing <0/> with your domain, such as <1/>. Nocturne will answer on that name and every site you create gets a subdomain under it, so pick something you are happy to keep. If you chose Folding@home above, add <2/> in front."

#~ msgid "If your domain is under duckdns.org, the installer asks early on for your DuckDNS token. <0>Nothing appears on screen as you paste it</0> – the token is hidden, and the installer tells you how many characters it read so you can see the paste landed. If DuckDNS does not accept it you can paste another. Press Enter with nothing pasted and it tells you the address to set yourself in <1>Step 3</1> instead. For any other domain, it prints the two records to create by hand. Either way it keeps working while the server boots, and waits for DNS before it requests certificates."
#~ msgstr "If your domain is under duckdns.org, the installer asks early on for your DuckDNS token. <0>Nothing appears on screen as you paste it</0> – the token is hidden, and the installer tells you how many characters it read so you can see the paste landed. If DuckDNS does not accept it you can paste another. Press Enter with nothing pasted and it tells you the address to set yourself in <1>Step 3</1> instead. For any other domain, it prints the two records to create by hand. Either way it keeps working while the server boots, and waits for DNS before it requests certificates."

#~ msgid "Skip this step if you gave the installer a DuckDNS token. For a DuckDNS name without one, sign in at duckdns.org, put the IP address the script printed into the <0>current ip</0> box next to your name and click <1>update ip</1>. For any other domain, create two <2>A</2> records at your domain provider, pointing at that address:"
#~ msgstr "Skip this step if you gave the installer a DuckDNS token. For a DuckDNS name without one, sign in at duckdns.org, put the IP address the script printed into the <0>current ip</0> box next to your name and click <1>update ip</1>. For any other domain, create two <2>A</2> records at your domain provider, pointing at that address:"

